WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:05.710
In this video, we're going to look at Unreal Engine's modeling tools

2
00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:09.710
and how we can use them to make some adjustment to the meshes in our project.

3
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:12.779
To start with, we'll look at the Xform tools,

4
00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:16.780
specifically the pivot tool and the split tool.

5
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.780
There are many useful tools in this category,

6
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:24.780
such as deforming, sculpting, remeshing, and creating entirely new geometry.

7
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.260
So because we had some difficulties

8
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:33.259
when importing our FBX from Unity as separate meshes,

9
00:00:33.259 --> 00:00:38.259
we are going to use the split tool before we use the pivot tool

10
00:00:38.259 --> 00:00:44.259
in order to be able to better work with our individual pillars.

11
00:00:44.259 --> 00:00:46.259
So in order to get to the modeling mode,

12
00:00:46.259 --> 00:00:48.259
we'll come over here to Selection,

13
00:00:48.259 --> 00:00:52.670
and instead we'll go here to Modeling or Shift 5.

14
00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.670
Now, you'll see this opens a new UI panel for us,

15
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.670
our viewport is getting smaller,

16
00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.670
and our outliner is getting kind of scrunched,

17
00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.670
and it's a little in the way.

18
00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.670
So this is where Unreal Engine's default layout starts

19
00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.670
to make a little bit more sense.

20
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:08.670
And because of that, I'm actually going to bring the outliner

21
00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.670
back over here onto the other side.

22
00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.439
But I'll leave the detail side open for now.

23
00:01:15.439 --> 00:01:17.439
So here we can see favorite tools,

24
00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:20.439
we can create our meshes, select different ones,

25
00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:24.439
select the faces of specific meshes and modify them.

26
00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:27.439
But I'm going to come here to Xform and Split.

27
00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:31.239
So as we can see now, it gives us a little preview

28
00:01:31.239 --> 00:01:35.239
of the mesh that we have selected

29
00:01:35.239 --> 00:01:38.239
and how it will be divided up into separate parts.

30
00:01:38.239 --> 00:01:41.239
We can see that the bottom and each one of these pillars

31
00:01:41.239 --> 00:01:45.239
is going to be put into a separate object.

32
00:01:45.239 --> 00:01:48.239
So I will hit, we can change how we want to split it up

33
00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:50.239
though over here, but I'm going to leave all of these

34
00:01:50.239 --> 00:01:52.239
as default for now.

35
00:01:52.239 --> 00:01:55.239
And thankfully it will transfer our materials as well.

36
00:01:55.239 --> 00:01:56.239
I'll hit Accept.

37
00:01:56.239 --> 00:02:03.900
And now we should see a new folder here called Generated.

38
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:09.900
And we see all of our new individual objects waiting for us.

39
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.530
We'll go ahead and save them all.

40
00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.680
Fantastic.

41
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.680
And now we can see that we can click

42
00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.680
on these, our individual pillars here.

43
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.969
The next thing we want to do though is Edit Pivot.

44
00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:39.500
Before we'll go, we can see that our pivot point

45
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.500
is actually right here in the middle

46
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.500
where it shares that, the one that we had

47
00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:47.500
with the bottom stage here.

48
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:54.039
So what we want to do is pick the first one,

49
00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:58.650
go Edit Pivot, we'll hit Bottom.

50
00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.479
Oh here it is, it was this one selected up here.

51
00:03:01.479 --> 00:03:04.860
We'll hit Bottom, we'll hit Accept.

52
00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:08.849
Fantastic.

53
00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:15.219
We can go to the next one, Edit Pivot, Bottom, Accept.

54
00:03:15.219 --> 00:03:23.860
We can also, if it makes sense for us,

55
00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.900
we go to Edit Pivot, we can also rotate

56
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.930
the direction that the pivot is facing.

57
00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.930
So if we want to have everything,

58
00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.930
have its inherent rotations that they were exported with

59
00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.930
now be baked into, or be visible in the outer transform

60
00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.930
versus baked in, we can do that.

61
00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.930
But for now, we'll just leave the transform

62
00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:45.930
as the default rotation.

63
00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:51.340
Oh, not split, excuse me, let's go back.

64
00:03:51.340 --> 00:04:03.789
Here we go, Edit Pivot, Bottom, Accept.

65
00:04:03.789 --> 00:04:06.789
And you can, if you can do this faster than me,

66
00:04:06.789 --> 00:04:18.269
feel free to hop to it.

67
00:04:18.269 --> 00:04:21.870
Oops, there we go.

68
00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:28.449
Last one, awesome.

69
00:04:28.449 --> 00:04:31.250
We'll make sure we save all of those.

70
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:42.149
However, we will notice though,

71
00:04:42.149 --> 00:04:45.790
that now that these are all separate objects,

72
00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.790
our BP session stage here still only has one,

73
00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:51.790
our old static mesh is a part of it.

74
00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:57.560
So in order to get these to be our new static meshes,

75
00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:00.750
we're going to delete that,

76
00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.750
come down here to our content drawer,

77
00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:07.750
our generated, and we can select all of these,

78
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.779
drag them in, check out our viewport.

79
00:05:10.779 --> 00:05:15.319
We'll hit compile, oop,

80
00:05:15.319 --> 00:05:17.319
but now they're all sitting on top of each other,

81
00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:21.319
so I might have hurt myself here.

82
00:05:21.319 --> 00:05:25.319
I'll give myself a reference for how we can

83
00:05:25.319 --> 00:06:07.050
bring them back and put them in their correct spots.

84
00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.050
I guess one probably needs to go over here,

85
00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:31.550
two will go over here, five,

86
00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:42.689
go up top, see how we did here.

87
00:06:42.689 --> 00:07:09.850
Try and get these close enough.

88
00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.850
Thankfully, we won't need to rebuild any of our logic

89
00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:15.850
because we're still just targeting our color MPC,

90
00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:23.990
and we're not targeting individual material objects.

91
00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:25.990
The next modeling mode feature we're going to take a look at

92
00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:28.990
is the UV project tool.

93
00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:30.990
There are a few different ways we can re-project

94
00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.990
the UVs back onto our static meshes,

95
00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.990
but in this case, we're going to use

96
00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:38.990
the box projection method,

97
00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:40.990
because that will give us a good look

98
00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.990
that I want to have on our boxes.

99
00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:46.699
We'll come here to our first cube,

100
00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:48.699
we'll go to project UVs,

101
00:07:48.699 --> 00:07:51.699
and here we can change from a plane projection

102
00:07:51.699 --> 00:07:53.860
to a box projection,

103
00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.860
and I also like to turn our box projection

104
00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:01.110
so it's roughly facing the same orientation,

105
00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.110
and that looks pretty good to me.

106
00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.110
If we twist it around though,

107
00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:07.459
we can see we get a little more control,

108
00:08:07.459 --> 00:08:11.459
and so maybe we can have it to where it's scrolling up on the inside.

109
00:08:11.459 --> 00:08:14.660
I think that'll look pretty good.

110
00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:15.660
We'll hit accept.

111
00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.100
Come to our next one.

112
00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.100
Project UVs, that looks correct out of the gate.

113
00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.100
Fantastic.

114
00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.990
We'll come over here.

115
00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:39.259
Project, accept.

116
00:08:39.259 --> 00:09:14.929
Last one, accept.

117
00:09:14.929 --> 00:09:18.929
And now we have them all flowing in the same direction

118
00:09:18.929 --> 00:09:23.440
centered around the center of our stage.

119
00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:30.460
In order to see our stage pillars changing color again,

120
00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.460
now that we have modified their UVs,

121
00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:42.909
we can delete all of these

122
00:09:42.909 --> 00:09:48.960
and drag in our blueprint,

123
00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:55.500
which now has the updated UVs for all of our assets.

124
00:09:55.500 --> 00:10:00.100
Get ourselves a little bit centered.

125
00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:03.899
Let's go back up and get it a little closer.

126
00:10:03.899 --> 00:10:16.450
Now when we press play again, there we go.

127
00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:22.460
In the next video, we'll start working with audio

128
00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:25.460
and adding sound cues to our level.
